# ============================================================
# corpus-tools .gitignore
# ============================================================
# Policy: this repo is a source-code + reproducibility repo, not
# a remote file store. Code, tests, docs, prompts, schemas, and
# manifests belong in git. Large/raw/generated data belongs in
# S3 with a row in manifests/s3_archive_manifest.jsonl.
#
# Reference policy: docs/2026-04-09_repos-reorg/2026-05-19_chatgpt-guide-to-file-types-to-exclude-in-repo.md
# Reference plan:   docs/2026-04-09_repos-reorg/2026-05-25_pare-down-log.md
# Reference rules:  AGENTS.md (Agents / Always require approval section)
# ============================================================


# ============================================================
# Canonical local-file mount points -- never commit
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Durable local-only files live under:
# /Users/randytrue/Documents/Code/_LOCAL_FILES/fof-mono/
#
# Worktrees expose the paths below as symlinks into that canonical
# folder. Keep these ignore rules in sync with the configured mount
# points so local files stay out of git even when a symlink is missing.
# ============================================================

# Data lake -- bulk of the historical bloat (~5.7 GB tracked)
# Git tracks the catalog/manifests/schemas/small samples, not the data.
/data
data/
!data/README.md
!data/manifests/
!data/manifests/**
!data/schemas/
!data/schemas/**
!data/samples/
!data/samples/**

# Exchange captures -- archived to S3, keep local-only.
/exchanges
/exchanges/

# Archive/log roots -- local/S3-backed state, not source.
_archive
_archive/
logs
logs/
*.log

# App-local data folders (_data).
# Any directory named _data is gitignored at any depth. Apps can
# add <app>/_data/ (or nested paths) for session DBs, fixtures, and
# other local-only assets without a per-app .gitignore entry.
**/_data
**/_data/
**/_data/**

# math-quiz keeps local run captures in math-quiz_data/ (per its README/AGENTS) —
# never commit them (real/test SQLite + JSON sessions live locally + in S3).
**/math-quiz_data
**/math-quiz_data/
**/math-quiz_data/**

# math-quiz: per-learner reward/completion animations (webp/gif) in _assets/.
# The whole folder is local-only and mounted from _LOCAL_FILES.
apps/math-quiz/_assets
apps/math-quiz/_assets/
apps/math-quiz/_assets/**
apps/math-quiz/dragon/assets/

# math-quiz: dragon local learner display-name map (and future local dragon data).
# Symlink mount from _LOCAL_FILES — explicit rule because data/ does not match the symlink itself.
apps/math-quiz/dragon/data
apps/math-quiz/dragon/data/
apps/math-quiz/dragon/data/**

# math-quiz: dragon playthrough apparatus run artifacts (sqlite, events.jsonl,
# screenshots) — the tracked reports live in dragon/playtests/*.md
apps/math-quiz/dragon/playtests/runs/

# Hermes config-sync freshness marker (local-only; drives sync_hermes_config.py --if-stale)
agents/*/.hermes_sync_state.json


# ============================================================
# Secrets and credentials -- never commit
# ============================================================
# .env files outside the repo's standard ignores
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Hardcoded config & credentials files referenced from README_internal.md
config.py
**/config.py
# content_studio's config module holds no secrets (model ids/thresholds only;
# API keys come from env vars) — track it despite the credential-file rule above.
!apps/content_studio/config.py
!apps/content_studio/model3d/config.py
!apps/minecraft/prism-sync/server/config.py
!apps/deutsch/content-tools/ctools/config.py
!apps/deutsch/content-forge/dforge/config.py
!apps/deutsch/content-redo/dredo/config.py
!apps/deutsch/deutsch-interject/dinterject/config.py
!apps/deutsch/worldview-mirror/wvmirror/config.py
credentials.json
credentials_new.json
gdrive_service_account.json
gdrive_service_account_fofgeneral20_personal.json
floodlamp-gdrive-jackie-cce56b4f953f.json
client_secret_*.*
client_secret_119941763167-c0oqkp63cv6elses4828p7fvthdqredv.apps.googleusercontent.com.json
client_secret_119941763167-jmob7gtcjbpamdukm8in6ekfp72r154h.apps.googleusercontent.com.json
# Local token / session caches
token.pickle
.sesskey
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
.aws/


# ============================================================
# PII safety net -- any file with PII in the name
# ============================================================
**/PII*
**/pii*
# public-snapshot tooling is code, not PII data — exempt from the pii* rule
!skills/repo-public/public-snapshot/pii-allowlist.md
!skills/repo-public/public-snapshot/scripts/pii_sweep.py
!skills/repo-ops/public-snapshot/pii-allowlist.md
!skills/repo-ops/public-snapshot/scripts/pii_sweep.py
# hash-store user hash logs (contain user PII); keep local-only, never commit
**/user_hash_log*
# Exception: the S3 PII *manifests* are a safe index -- they record only repo paths,
# sizes, sha256 checksums, and S3 keys/status, never any PII row content. Track them so
# the [S3-BUCKET] bucket has a versioned catalog. (The PII data files themselves stay ignored.)
!manifests/pii_*.manifest.jsonl


